{"id": "q0002", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1165022308, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "Aiden is making his famous steakhouse-seasoned meatballs for a neighborhood cookout. He adds two tablespoons of his secret steakhouse seasoning for every pound of ground beef he uses. He gets sixteen meatballs from each pound of meat. If he wants to make 80 meatballs for the cookout, how much of his secret seasoning will he need?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0002.wav", "input_sha256": "fec12bcf750c0246a49dd7730c9816c40f1eb1a4633fc590eb361ac4309c3ce9", "input_samples": 387400, "input_s": 24.212, "n_real_chunks": 25, "score": 0.284, "act": 0.9984, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "80 meatballs ÷ 16 meatballs per pound = 5 pounds of ground beef 2 tablespoons seasoning per pound × 5 pounds = 10 tablespoons Final answer: 10", "expert_answer": "80 meatballs ÷ 16 meatballs per pound = 5 pounds of ground beef\n\n2 tablespoons seasoning per pound × 5 pounds = 10 tablespoons\n\n**Final answer: 10**", "transcript": "Aiden is making his famous steakhouse seasoned meatballs for a neighborhood cookout. He adds 2 tablespoons of his secret steakhouse seasoning for every pound of ground beef he uses. He gets 16 meatballs from each pound of meat. If he wants to make 80 meatballs for the cookout, how much of his secret", "asr_s": 4.24, "expert_s": 1.93, "expert_input_samples": 387400, "expert_input_s": 24.212, "expert_input_sha256": "fec12bcf750c0246a49dd7730c9816c40f1eb1a4633fc590eb361ac4309c3ce9", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 2.047, "relay_synth_ms": 86