{"id": "q0191", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 209278112, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "An uncle owns his property in fee simple. The uncle executes and delivers a deed to the property with the following granting clause:\"To my nephew and my niece for the life of my nephew, then to my gardener. \"As a result of the grant, which of the following is the most accurate statement regarding the ownership rights of the property?\n\nA. The nephew has a life estate pur autre vie, the niece has a vested remainder, and the gardener has a life estate.\nB. The nephew and niece are tenants in common for the life of the first of them to die, the nephew and niece have contingent remainders in fee simple defeasible, and the gardener has an executory interest.\nC. The nephew and niece are joint tenants with rights of survivorship, and the gardener has a contingent remainder.\nD. The nephew and niece are tenants in common, and the gardener has a vested remainder in fee simple.\nE. The nephew and niece are joint tenants in fee simple defeasible, and the gardener has an executory interest.\nF. The nephew has a vested remainder, the niece has a life estate, and the gardener has a life estate pur autre vie.\nG. The nephew and niece both have life estates pur autre vie, and the gardener has a contingent remainder.\nH. The nephew has a life estate, the niece has a life estate pur autre vie, and the gardener has a vested remainder.\nI. The nephew has a life estate, the niece has a vested remainder, and the gardener has a life estate pur autre vie.\nJ. The nephew has a life estate, the niece also has a life estate, and the gardener has a vested remainder.\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0191.wav", "input_sha256": "edbd85c13447bda5711b21ce75bf5807268cd8f25c91ed6158edad1b1a5e98e8", "input_samples": 1574800, "input_s": 98.425, "n_real_chunks": 99, "score": 0.7324, "act": 0.9994, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "H. The nephew has a life estate, the niece has a life estate pur autre vie, and the gardener has a vested remainder.", "expert_answer": "**H. The nephew has a life estate, the niece has a life estate pur autre vie, and the gardener has a vested remainder.**", "transcript": "An uncle owns his property in fee simple. The uncle executes and delivers a deed to the property with the following granting clause: to my nephew and my niece for the life of my nephew, then to my gardener. As a result of the grant, which of the following is the most accurate statement regarding the", "asr_s": 4.48, "expert_s": 4.5, "expert_input_samples": 1574800, "expert_input_s": 98.425, "expert_input_sha256": "edbd85c13447bda5711b21ce75bf5807268cd8f25c91ed6158edad1b1a5e98e8", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 7.482, "relay_synth_ms": 4882, "onset_chunk": 98, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 281, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 281, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0191_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "34da47cf441dc65817f000ac22d15396a2d7541d64e8653d8e24bbba02557e25", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 7.96}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0191_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "156ede4061b254b6b896c70ba42fe632a7dcdfa303f0fdbdeedb0a3105a743e0", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0191_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "f7705f747d2bd4ec8ab9c8eeea427aafe19ae1922f4e4e5d361a3f0b1db0b22b", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.071, 1.133, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.081, 2.144, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.082, 3.148, 1, 0, 0], [3