{"id": "q0406", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1158985889, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "What is Pickleball?", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0406.wav", "input_sha256": "67a862b71bc40e0a6a206966690b7b8a9331d4abf19002edbce08979f182b8a5", "input_samples": 16800, "input_s": 1.05, "n_real_chunks": 2, "score": 0.1279, "act": 0.997, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Pickleball is a paddle sport that combines elements of tennis, badminton, and table tennis. It’s played on a small court with a solid paddle and a lightweight plastic ball with holes, usually as singles or doubles. Key features: Played over a net on a court similar in size to a badminton court , Uses an underhand serve , Has a “kitchen” or non-volley zone near the net , Popular because it’s easy to learn, social, and lower-impact than tennis", "expert_answer": "**Pickleball** is a paddle sport that combines elements of **tennis, badminton, and table tennis**. It’s played on a small court with a **solid paddle** and a **lightweight plastic ball with holes**, usually as singles or doubles.\n\nKey features:\n- Played over a net on a court similar in size to a badminton court\n- Uses an underhand serve\n- Has a “kitchen” or non-volley zone near the net\n- Popular because it’s easy to learn, social, and lower-impact than tennis", "transcript": "What is pickleball?\n", "asr_s": 0.71, "expert_s": 2.71, "expert_input_samples": 16800, "expert_input_s": 1.05, "expert_input_sha256": "67a862b71bc40e0a6a206966690b7b8a9331d4abf19002edbce08979f182b8a5", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 2.994, "relay_synth_ms": 15845, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 85, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 85, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0406_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "dda513ffa71f5a3e061d500ee0ded5a05d405fca7eef71a6a7b8b3b19333ef4c", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 26.56}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0406_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "c30a7efa6c6d3955551bc6c38ab101ad655699231024569b2885647531ba3bff", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0406_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "c88881c0c3c14eeb5a667c2630cdaafa19852ff817bd0af1cc157325080d84d0", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 0.52}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.075, 1.135, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 1.05, 1.208, 1.267, 1, 0, 0], [2, 0, 2.05, 2.128, 2.191, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.05, 3.127, 3.817, 0, 24000, 0]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 1.05, "last_real_feed_done": 1.208, "onset": 3.817, "gate_read_done": 3.817, "fire": 3.817, "candidate_first_pcm": 3.817, "stall_note": 3.818, "stall_first_pcm": 4.243, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 4.243, "expert_req": 3.818, "expert_resp": 7.237, "relay_synth_start": 7.237, "relay_first_pcm": 8.081, "relay_synth_end": 23.082, "first_any_pcm": 3.817, "first_answer_pcm": 8.081, "session_end": 23.273}, "ttfa_answer_s": 7.031, "ttfa_any_s": 2.767}
{"id": "q0425", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3995831193, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "Provide a bulleted list of things to think about when buying a house", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0425.wav", "input_sha256": "9e6324dca26b1ad3031b2273503cffcd44dcf8caad3c270cbc37b8ffa7bf4a9d", "input_samples": 62400, "input_s": 3.9, "n_real_chunks": 4, "score": 0.5081, "act": 0.9951, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Budget: Know what you can afford, including down payment, monthly mortgage, taxes, insurance, utilities, and maintenance. , Mortgage options: Compare interest rates, loan types, terms, and lender fees. , Location: Consider commute, neighborhood safety, schools, public transit, shopping, and future development. , Home condition: Look at the roof, foundation, plumbing, electrical system, HVAC,.", "expert_answer": "- **Budget:** Know what you can afford, including down payment, monthly mortgage, taxes, insurance, utilities, and maintenance.\n\n- **Mortgage options:** Compare interest rates, loan types, terms, and lender fees.\n\n- **Location:** Consider commute, neighborhood safety, schools, public transit, shopping, and future development.\n\n- **Home condition:** Look at the roof, foundation, plumbing, electrical system, HVAC, windows, and overall maintenance.\n\n- **Inspection:** Hire a qualified home inspector before committing.\n\n- **Property taxes and insurance:** Check annual property taxes and whether special insurance is needed, such as flood or earthquake coverage.\n\n- **HOA rules and fees:** If applicable, review homeowners association fees, restrictions, reserves, and rules.\n\n- **Resale value:** Consider whether the home will likely appeal to future buyers.\n\n- **Size and layout:** Make sure the number of bedrooms, bathrooms, storage, and living spaces fit your current and future needs.\n\n- **Lot and exterior:** Evaluate yard size, drainage, landscaping, parking, fencing, and exterior upkeep.\n\n- **Repairs and renovations:** Estimate costs for immediate fixes or desired upgrades.\n\n- **Utilities and efficiency:** Check heating/cooling costs, insulation, appliances, windows, and energy efficiency.\n\n- **Local market conditions:** Understand whether it is a buyer’s or seller’s market and how quickly homes are selling.\n\n- **Legal/title issues:** Ensure the title is clear and review easements, liens, boundaries, and disclosures.\n\n- **Future plans:** Think about how long you expect to live there and whether the home fits your lifestyle over time.", "transcript": "Provide a bulleted list of things to think about when buying a house.\n", "asr_s": 0.45, "expert_s": 6.35, "expert_input_samples": 62400, "expert_input_s": 3.9, "expert_input_sha256": "9e6324dca26b1ad3031b2273503cffcd44dcf8caad3c270cbc37b8ffa7bf4a9d", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 5.982, "relay_synth_ms": 13897, "onset_chunk": 4, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0425_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "261b784336049e2d3c18128739758f712985bcd86b85611d80592c76131b7758", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 24.52}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0425_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "1ce36f3cdd220c8acc014753dee1e27a98b3ddefa5f096faf8e3e66fc1731fc8", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0425_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "978ad71e962adde0e9fa32a39226009a690b82324bb6a616f151d01ec11bd894", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.08, 1.146, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.08, 2.143, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.08, 3.143, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 3.9, 3.977, 4.04, 1, 0, 0], [4, 0, 4.9, 4.979, 5.486, 0, 24000, 0]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 3.9, "last_real_feed_done": 3.977, "onset": 5.486, "gate_read_done": 5.487, "fire": 5.487, "candidate_first_pcm": 5.486, "stall_note": 5.488, "stall_first_pcm": 6.312, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 6.312, "expert_req": 5.488, "expert_resp": 12.294, "relay_synth_start": 12.295, "relay_first_pcm": 13.116, "relay_synth_end": 26.192, "first_any_pcm": 5.486, "first_answer_pcm": 13.116, "session_end": 26.367}, "ttfa_answer_s": 9.216, "ttfa_any_s": 1.586}
{"id": "q0450", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3506498001, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "When did google first start?", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0450.wav", "input_sha256": "1f29d3198a158e8ec46c8485dc58a5bb9141a6afa38c1e2f71de073f900cc378", "input_samples": 25800, "input_s": 1.613, "n_real_chunks": 2, "score": 0.3654, "act": 0.9948, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Google first started in 1998. More specifically, Google was incorporated as a company on September 4, 1998, by Larry Page and Sergey Brin.", "expert_answer": "Google first started in **1998**.\n\nMore specifically, Google was incorporated as a company on **September 4, 1998**, by **Larry Page and Sergey Brin**.", "transcript": "When did Google first start?\n", "asr_s": 0.4, "expert_s": 1.68, "expert_input_samples": 25800, "expert_input_s": 1.613, "expert_input_sha256": "1f29d3198a158e8ec46c8485dc58a5bb9141a6afa38c1e2f71de073f900cc378", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 0.869, "relay_synth_ms": 6095, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 439, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 439, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0450_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "c0347d6df24347eb26a91e0a39f497aaa7df551b3eec50ca41c50de218894abc", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 10.28}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0450_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "6056195ea1f740657a8d6db12f472f3a1e42509a633d6023008985bbff52bd6e", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0450_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "ecf3ce2e76662037aded9248322df274c60f84124e3483b3d19b6dbbed190afd", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.88}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.07, 1.132, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 1.613, 1.691, 1.754, 1, 0, 0], [2, 0, 2.612, 2.69, 2.752, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.612, 3.689, 4.414, 0, 24000, 0], [4, 0, 4.612, 5.129, 5.624, 0, 21120, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 1.613, "last_real_feed_done": 1.691, "onset": 4.414, "gate_read_done": 4.414, "fire": 4.414, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.414, "stall_note": 4.415, "stall_first_pcm": 5.052, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 5.624, "expert_req": 4.414, "expert_resp": 6.493, "relay_synth_start": 6.493, "relay_first_pcm": 7.313, "relay_synth_end": 12.588, "first_any_pcm": 4.414, "first_answer_pcm": 7.313, "session_end": 12.752}, "ttfa_answer_s": 5.701, "ttfa_any_s": 2.801}
{"id": "q0467", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1682517937, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "What are some cardio machines at the gym?", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0467.wav", "input_sha256": "a348a140bd17f1135123fedb6faf5f2e340311b8be04fb503e92e3c28e12c144", "input_samples": 39400, "input_s": 2.462, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.3433, "act": 0.9942, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Some common cardio machines at the gym include: Treadmill — walking, jogging, or running , Elliptical machine — low-impact full-body cardio , Stationary bike — upright or recumbent cycling , Stair climber / StairMaster — simulates climbing stairs , Rowing machine — cardio plus back, legs, and arms , Spin bike — indoor cycling, often used in classes , Arc trainer — low-impact cardio similar to an elliptical , SkiErg — mimics cross-country skiing , Assault bike / air bike — uses both arms and legs with fan resistance , Jacob’s ladder — climbing-style cardio machine", "expert_answer": "Some common **cardio machines at the gym** include:\n\n- **Treadmill** — walking, jogging, or running\n- **Elliptical machine** — low-impact full-body cardio\n- **Stationary bike** — upright or recumbent cycling\n- **Stair climber / StairMaster** — simulates climbing stairs\n- **Rowing machine** — cardio plus back, legs, and arms\n- **Spin bike** — indoor cycling, often used in classes\n- **Arc trainer** — low-impact cardio similar to an elliptical\n- **SkiErg** — mimics cross-country skiing\n- **Assault bike / air bike** — uses both arms and legs with fan resistance\n- **Jacob’s ladder** — climbing-style cardio machine", "transcript": "What are some cardio machines at the gym?\n", "asr_s": 1.0, "expert_s": 5.35, "expert_input_samples": 39400, "expert_input_s": 2.462, "expert_input_sha256": "a348a140bd17f1135123fedb6faf5f2e340311b8be04fb503e92e3c28e12c144", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 5.552, "relay_synth_ms": 27587, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0467_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "e9eaa192d692b5d679fb6f638e19927f4518e829c6e8685d30cb9570dff2f33b", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 48.4}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0467_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "6e6a97cb7c634b02a05c2d17c880de86b600126ef1b2ffb80915b23dbdace3fc", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0467_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "af5555f4d4e85d9d7331cd317cabee7bfbf2be776ba65ca23a271f02219858d6", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.077, 1.139, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.074, 2.136, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 2.462, 2.541, 2.602, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.462, 3.54, 4.04, 0, 24000, 0]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 2.462, "last_real_feed_done": 2.541, "onset": 4.04, "gate_read_done": 4.041, "fire": 4.041, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.04, "stall_note": 4.041, "stall_first_pcm": 4.844, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 4.844, "expert_req": 4.041, "expert_resp": 10.395, "relay_synth_start": 10.396, "relay_first_pcm": 11.242, "relay_synth_end": 37.984, "first_any_pcm": 4.04, "first_answer_pcm": 11.242, "session_end": 38.232}, "ttfa_answer_s": 8.78, "ttfa_any_s": 1.578}
{"id": "q0485", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 348414739, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "为一个蛋糕烘焙业务创建一个使命宣言。", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0485.wav", "input_sha256": "96872ba43093364f6661e62e870c5d9e3f443ebf800656642e4cb4ef3579a748", "input_samples": 63200, "input_s": 3.95, "n_real_chunks": 4, "score": 0.2573, "act": 0.9963, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "使命宣言： 我们致力于用优质原料、精湛工艺和真诚服务，烘焙美味、精致且充满温度的蛋糕，为每一位顾客的生日、庆典与日常时刻增添甜蜜与幸福。", "expert_answer": "**使命宣言：**  \n我们致力于用优质原料、精湛工艺和真诚服务，烘焙美味、精致且充满温度的蛋糕，为每一位顾客的生日、庆典与日常时刻增添甜蜜与幸福。", "transcript": "为一个蛋糕烘焙业务创建一个使命宣言。\n", "asr_s": 0.51, "expert_s": 2.54, "expert_input_samples": 63200, "expert_input_s": 3.95, "expert_input_sha256": "96872ba43093364f6661e62e870c5d9e3f443ebf800656642e4cb4ef3579a748", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 1.953, "relay_synth_ms": 8943, "onset_chunk": 4, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 364, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 364, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0485_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "1fcddc97b9597084842b08c6d44f65a41fcb06a4f1827785841cb5c16efed4fc", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 15.24}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0485_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "6ff74aa0d8c21bdbe509e0ac6adc6e021baf9a692555e39cf57608e6160262d0", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0485_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "b8e18e0ca8523ecd8ace727f4783fa73352035a2a1ac2ac3cafa36e13822435d", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.44}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.079, 1.145, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.078, 2.137, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.075, 3.135, 